      font-family: 'Inter', -apple-system, sans-serif !important;
      font-size: 11px !important;
      font-weight: 700 !important;
      color: #8A6A23 !important;
      text-transform: uppercase !important;
      letter-spacing: .08em !important;
      margin-bottom: 8px !important;
      display: block !important;
    }
    .roam-field-note-quote {
      font-family: 'Inter', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif !important;
      font-style: italic !important;
      font-size: 15px !important;
      line-height: 1.65 !important;
      color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.8) !important;
      margin: 0 0 10px !important;
    }
    .roam-field-note-author {
      font-family: 'Inter', -apple-system, sans-serif !important;
      font-size: 11px !important;
      font-weight: 700 !important;
      color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55) !important;
      text-transform: uppercase !important;
      letter-spacing: .06em !important;
      margin: 0 !important;
    }
  
  </style>

  <main class="roam-tour-main" style="padding: 120px 24px 80px;">
  <div class="roam-tour-wrapper">
    <div class="roam-tour-badge">1-DAY PRIVATE EXCURSION // ATLAS &amp; CINEMA STUDIOS</div>
    <h1 class="roam-tour-title">Morocco Film Location Tour: Ait Benhaddou &amp; Atlas Studios</h1>
    
    <div class="roam-tour-meta-bar">
      <span class="roam-tour-meta-item">📍 START/FINISH: MARRAKECH</span>
      <span class="roam-tour-meta-item">⏱ DURATION: FULL DAY (11-12 HRS)</span>
      <span class="roam-tour-meta-item">🏛 UNESCO: KASBAH AIT BENHADDOU</span>
      <span class="roam-tour-meta-item">🛡 100% PRIVATE 4X4 TRANSPORT &amp; DRIVER</span>
    </div>

    <!-- GEO & AEO Tour Fast Facts (BLUF) -->
    <aside class="ai-quick-summary-card" aria-label="Tour Fast Facts and Summary">
      <div class="ai-summary-header">
        <span class="ai-summary-kicker">⚡ TOUR AT A GLANCE (QUICK SUMMARY)</span>
        <span class="ai-summary-badge">Full-Day Private Departure</span>
      </div>
      <p class="ai-summary-text">
        The <strong>Heritage &amp; Cinema Day Excursion</strong> is a full-day private journey (11–12 hours) departing Marrakech at 07:30 AM. Crossing the dramatic High Atlas Mountains via the Tizi n'Tichka pass (2,260m), the itinerary visits the UNESCO World Heritage mudbrick ksar of <strong>Ait Benhaddou</strong> (filming location for <em>Gladiator</em> and <em>Game of Thrones</em>) and the <strong>Atlas Film Studios</strong> in Ouarzazate. Private pricing starts at <strong>€380 per vehicle (1–4 passengers)</strong>, including private air-conditioned 4x4 or minivan transport, licensed driver-guide, fuel, all highway tolls, and direct door-to-door riad pickup.
      </p>
    </aside>

    <div style="margin-bottom: 40px; border: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.12); overflow: hidden;">
      <img src="/images/pol-kasbah.jpg" alt="Kasbah Ait Benhaddou and Ouarzazate Tour" style="width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 520px; object-fit: cover; display: block;">
    </div>

    <div class="roam-article-body">
      <p style="font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 500; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 28px;">Embark on the ultimate journey through Morocco's cinematic history and ancient caravan routes. The <strong>Heritage &amp; Cinema Tour</strong> takes you across the spectacular High Atlas Mountains to explore legendary Kasbahs, including the iconic <strong>Ait Benhaddou</strong>, and the <strong>Ouarzazate film studios</strong>—the true Hollywood of Africa.</p>

      <h2>Why Take an Ait Benhaddou Tour?</h2>
      <p>If you are researching the best <strong>Morocco day trips</strong> from Marrakech, an <strong>Ait Benhaddou tour</strong> is an essential rite of passage. Designated as a UNESCO World Heritage site since 1987, the fortified clay village (Ksar) of Ait Benhaddou represents the apex of southern Moroccan earthen architecture. Wandering through its towering red-earthen gates feels like stepping hundreds of years back into the trans-Saharan salt and gold caravan era.</p>
      
      <p>Beyond its deep historical roots, Ait Benhaddou is a global cinematic pilgrimage. If you have ever wanted to visit the real-world filming sets of <em>Gladiator</em>, <em>Game of Thrones</em> (the yellow city of Yunkai), <em>Lawrence of Arabia</em>, or <em>Kingdom of Heaven</em>, this private expedition brings those legendary scenes to life.</p>

      <!-- Highlights Box -->
      <div class="roam-highlights-box">
        <h3 class="roam-highlights-title">Tour Highlights</h3>
        <ul class="roam-highlight-list">
          <li>
            <span class="roam-highlight-bullet">✦</span>
            <div><strong>Tizi n'Tichka Mountain Pass:</strong> Cross the High Atlas at 2,260m elevation with dramatic stops at scenic mountain lookouts.</div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="roam-highlight-bullet">✦</span>
            <div><strong>UNESCO Kasbah Ait Benhaddou:</strong> In-depth private guided walking tour of the ancient mudbrick granaries and towers.</div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="roam-highlight-bullet">✦</span>
            <div><strong>Atlas Film Studios:</strong> Go behind the scenes at the world's largest desert film lot in Ouarzazate.</div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="roam-highlight-bullet">✦</span>
            <div><strong>Kasbah Taourirt:</strong> Discover the restored 19th-century Glaoui palace decorated with intricate stucco and cedar woodwork.</div>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2>Detailed Day-Trip Itinerary</h2>

      <RouteGoogleMapCard
        origin="Marrakech"
        destination="Ait Ben Haddou"
        distance="185 km"
        duration="3h 45m"
        highway="N9 via Tizi n'Tichka Pass (2,260m)"
        price={380}
        waUrl="https://wa.me/212760426269?text=Salam%20Roam%20Morocco!%20I'd%20like%20to%20book%20the%20Morocco%20Film%20Location%20Tour%20(Ait%20Benhaddou%20%26%20Ouarzazate)."
      />

      <div class="roam-itinerary-card">
        <span class="roam-day-badge">LEG 01 // 07:30 AM DEPARTURE</span>
        <h3 class="roam-itinerary-title">Crossing the High Atlas Mountains via Tizi n'Tichka</h3>
        <p class="roam-itinerary-desc">Your private driver picks you up from your Marrakech riad in a comfortable, climate-controlled 4x4 or executive Mercedes van. Ascend the twisting engineering marvel of the Tizi n'Tichka pass (2,260m). Stop for sweeping photos across deep valleys, dramatic gorges, and red-clay Berber hamlets clinging to the mountainsides.</p>
        <div class="roam-field-note">
          <span class="roam-field-note-kicker">Field Note // Tizi n'Tichka Summit (2,260m)</span>
          <p class="roam-field-note-quote">&ldquo;At the cold, windy pass where commercial minivans race past to shave twenty minutes off their drive, there is a stone shelter where Daoud bakes round khobz bread buried under hot olive charcoal. We stop. Daoud hands you bread so warm you have to toss it from hand to hand, paired with peppery unfiltered mountain olive oil. That single bite at two thousand meters explains why you take the high road.&rdquo;</p>
          <p class="roam-field-note-author">&mdash; Brahim, Roam Morocco Route Specialist</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="roam-itinerary-card">
        <span class="roam-day-badge">LEG 02 // MIDDAY EXPLORATION</span>
        <h3 class="roam-itinerary-title">Kasbah Ait Benhaddou UNESCO World Heritage Site</h3>
        <p class="roam-itinerary-desc">Cross the shallow Ounila River stepping-stones to enter Ait Benhaddou. With your private local expert, explore the ancient granary atop the hill, navigate the maze of earthen passageways, and admire the defensive towers that stood watch over historic desert merchants. Enjoy a panoramic lunch on a shaded terrace facing the fortress.</p>
        <div class="roam-field-note">
          <span class="roam-field-note-kicker">Field Note // Inside the Upper Ksar</span>
          <p class="roam-field-note-quote">&ldquo;Tour groups take three photos by the Roman arena set and turn back. But if you climb the mudbrick switchbacks to the upper granary where Mokhtar and just four families still live, Mokhtar paints desert scenes using saffron, tea, and cobalt indigo—then holds the paper over a gas flame so the sugar browns into golden caramel. The scent of scorched sugar, river mud, and baking sun is the true soul of this place.&rdquo;</p>
          <p class="roam-field-note-author">&mdash; Brahim, Roam Morocco Route Specialist</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="roam-itinerary-card">
        <span class="roam-day-badge">LEG 03 // AFTERNOON CINEMA</span>
        <h3 class="roam-itinerary-title">Ouarzazate: Atlas Film Studios &amp; Kasbah Taourirt</h3>
        <p class="roam-itinerary-desc">Drive 30 minutes south into Ouarzazate, the gateway to the Sahara. Tour the famous Atlas Film Studios where sets from Cleopatra, Kingdom of Heaven, and Gladiator stand preserved in the desert sun. Tour the labyrinthine chambers of Kasbah Taourirt before relaxing on your private evening drive back to Marrakech.</p>
        <div class="roam-field-note">
          <span class="roam-field-note-kicker">Field Note // Atlas Studios Backlot</span>
          <p class="roam-field-note-quote">&ldquo;Standing in front of a crumbling fiberglass Egyptian temple in the middle of the Moroccan desert should feel ridiculous, but it doesn&rsquo;t. You meet elders here who worked as extras for David Lean in 1962 and Ridley Scott in 2000. They speak four languages, have died on camera thirty times, and return home every night to irrigate date palms. Morocco holds cinema and antiquity in the very same hand.&rdquo;</p>
          <p class="roam-field-note-author">&mdash; Brahim, Roam Morocco Route Specialist</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions: Ait Benhaddou &amp; Ouarzazate</h2>
      
      <div style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <h3 style="font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 19px; font-weight: 800; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;">What movies were filmed at Ait Benhaddou?</h3>
        <p>Over 20 Hollywood blockbusters and prestige television series have filmed at Ait Benhaddou. Key titles include Ridley Scott's <em>Gladiator</em> (1999) and <em>Gladiator II</em> (2024), <em>Game of Thrones</em> (Season 3 as Yunkai), <em>The Mummy</em>, <em>Kingdom of Heaven</em>, <em>Prince of Persia</em>, and David Lean's timeless masterpiece <em>Lawrence of Arabia</em>.</p>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <h3 style="font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 19px; font-weight: 800; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;">How long is the drive from Marrakech to Ait Benhaddou?</h3>
        <p>The distance is approximately 180 km (112 miles), taking about 3.5 to 4 hours each way. Because the route traverses the high mountain passes of the Atlas, having an experienced private chauffeur allows you to relax, stop whenever you wish for coffee and photography, and avoid the stress of rental car navigation.</p>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <h3 style="font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 19px; font-weight: 800; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px;">Can I extend this into a multi-day Sahara tour?</h3>
        <p>Absolutely! Ait Benhaddou is the natural first gateway on the road to the Merzouga Sahara sand dunes (Erg Chebbi). We frequently customize this itinerary into a 3-day or 4-day private desert expedition with luxury glamping.</p>
      </div>

